   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## A generated model as a height map\n\n**kubakub scene render** gives the projection view of your real building (empty = the sample building). **kubakub form height** draws a 3D model from the same camera and takes the real wall away: black = the wall, white = where a form stands furthest out.\n\n1. Lay the generated model onto the real one with **kubakub align 3d model** (example `align_3d_model.json`); give it the same model file as `template_file` that scene render reads.\n2. Paste the aligned file into `model_file` here, or connect its `model`. Empty = a sample form.\n3. Raise `wall_m` until the wall is black.\n\nThe height is a picture: bring it up from black and the forms grow out of the wall (kubakub mask animate, the director), `depth` goes into the depth shaders (hard shadow, sheet of light) or a displacement in Houdini or Blender."
   ],
   "title": "Read me"
  }
